Because $28 \div \blue{4} = \green{7}
$ ,
$
\qquad \begin{eqnarray}
i ^ {28} &=& (i^\blue{4})^\green{7}
\\
&=& (1)^\green{7}
\\
&=&
1
\end{eqnarray}
$

Because $10 \div \blue{4} = \green{2}
\text{ remainder } \red{2}$ ,
$
\qquad \begin{eqnarray}
i ^ {10} &=& (i^\blue{4})^\green{2}
\cdot i^\red{2} \\
&=& (1)^\green{2}
\cdot i^\red{2} \\
&=& i^\red{2}
\end{eqnarray}
$

Because $24 \div \blue{4} = \green{6}
$ ,
$
\qquad \begin{eqnarray}
i ^ {24} &=& (i^\blue{4})^\green{6}
\\
&=& (1)^\green{6}
\\
&=&
1
\end{eqnarray}
$

Because $6 \div \blue{4} = \green{1}
\text{ remainder } \red{2}$ ,
$
\qquad \begin{eqnarray}
i ^ {6} &=& (i^\blue{4})^\green{1}
\cdot i^\red{2} \\
&=& (1)^\green{1}
\cdot i^\red{2} \\
&=& i^\red{2}
\end{eqnarray}
$

